  step=2,desc:stand M — turn it to 10 — mark it fork — and fork N from the mark,dige:f799380238c97c6b
  step=3,desc:both turn to 13 — then hands — perch 2 is caught from N — carp 3 is said born 11 in M and 12 in N,dige:2c55ea3da2641836
  step=4,desc:merge N into M,dige:4e72f76da41ce2ba
    Assertion:what-only-n-changed,sentence:what only N changed comes across — the perch caught from N is gone from M
    Assertion:what-both-changed-differently,sentence:what both changed differently is refused with both sides said — M keeps its own carp
    Assertion:what-both-did-alike,sentence:what both did alike is kept once — the eggs both hatched and laid are not doubled
